# Notification System Fixes & Improvements Summary

This document summarizes the debugging and implementation work done to fix the notification system, including deep linking for comments and missing notifications for Weave requests.

## 1. 404 Errors on Notification API
**Issue:** The frontend was requesting `/notifications` but the backend registered the route as `/notification`.
**Fix:** Updated [server/src/api.ts](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/server/src/api.ts) to match the plural form.

```typescript
// server/src/api.ts
import notificationsRouter from "./notifications";

// Fixed route path
router.use("/notifications", notificationsRouter);
```

## 2. Navbar Unread Badge Synchronization
**Issue:** The navbar unread count didn't update when notifications were marked as read on the Notifications page.
**Fix:** implemented a custom event system to sync state across components.

**Frontend ([components/Notification.tsx](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/client/app/components/Notification.tsx)):** Dispatch event when reading.
```tsx
// Dispatch global event after marking read
window.dispatchEvent(new Event('notification_update'));
```

**Frontend ([components/Navbar.tsx](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/client/app/components/Navbar.tsx)):** Listen for event and re-fetch.
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
    const handleLocalUpdate = () => {
        // Re-fetch unread count...
    };
    window.addEventListener('notification_update', handleLocalUpdate);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('notification_update', handleLocalUpdate);
}, []);
```

## 3. Comment Deep Linking & Auto-Scroll
**Issue:** Clicking a comment notification didn't scroll to the specific comment, especially if it was inside a collapsed tab (e.g., specific item tab).
**Fix:** Implemented full deep linking support.

**Backend ([server/src/comments.ts](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/server/src/comments.ts)):**
1. Added anchor hash to notification links.
```typescript
link: `/item/${post_id}#comment-${newComment.id}`
```
2. Added endpoint to look up which item/tab a comment belongs to.
```typescript
// GET /comments/:id
router.get("/:id", async (req, res) => {
    // Returns comment details including item_id
});
```

**Frontend ([CommentSection.tsx](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/client/app/components/Comment/CommentSection.tsx)):** Handle URL hash on load.
```tsx
// Check for #comment-ID hash
const handleDeepLink = async () => {
    const hash = window.location.hash;
    if (hash && hash.startsWith("#comment-")) {
        const commentId = hash.substring(9);
        // 1. Fetch check which tab this comment is in
        const res = await fetch(`.../api/comments/${commentId}`);
        // 2. Switch to that tab
        setActiveTab(targetTab); 
        // 3. Scroll to element after render
        setTimeout(() => {
             document.getElementById(commentId).scrollIntoView(...);
        }, 500);
    }
};
```

**Frontend ([CommentItem.tsx](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/client/app/components/Comment/CommentItem.tsx)):** Add ID to DOM element.
```tsx
<div id={`comment-${comment.id}`} className="...">
    {/* Comment content */}
</div>
```

## 4. Weave Notification Fixes
**Issue A: Missing Notifications (Schema Validation)**
`z.url()` was rejecting relative paths like `/profile/123`.
**Fix:** Relaxed validation in [server/src/utils/notificationService.ts](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/server/src/utils/notificationService.ts).
```typescript
// Changed from z.url() to z.string()
link: z.string().optional().nullable(),
```

**Issue B: Missing Notifications (ID Type Mismatch)**
Notifications weren't sending because strictly comparing string `userId` (from session) with number [id](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/client/app/contexts/NavBarContext.tsx#16-50) (from DB) failed.
**Fix:** Cast ID to number in [server/src/weaves.ts](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/server/src/weaves.ts).
```typescript
// Ensure ID is a number for comparison
const initiatorId = Number(req.user!.userId);
const targetUserId = (initiatorId === giverId) ? receiverId : giverId;
```

**Issue C: Socket.IO Instance Access**
`req.app.get("io")` was returning undefined in the Weave endpoint context.
**Fix:** Used `res.locals.io` which is reliably set by middleware in [server/src/weaves.ts](file:///Users/zhangjunhao/Desktop/Git-repos/Megaweave/server/src/weaves.ts).
```typescript
// Use res.locals to access socket instance
const io = res.locals.io;
```

**Issue D: Correct Message Content**
Notifications were generic.
**Fix:** Differentiated between 'Wish' and 'Share' post types.
```typescript
if (postType === 'wish') {
  notifTitle = "New Share Offer"; 
  notifContent = `${initiatorName} wants to share...`;
} else {
  notifTitle = "New Wish Request";
  notifContent = `${initiatorName} is wishing for...`;
}
```
